<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Osceola</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1804–1838</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Osceola was a Seminole war leader who led resistance to removal from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-seminole-war">Second Seminole War</a>. In 1837 he was seized by American troops while meeting them under a flag of truce, an act widely condemned. He died in prison at Fort Moultrie in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-carolina">South Carolina</a> in 1838 and became a lasting symbol of Native resistance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/osceola.jpg" alt="Osceola" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Catlin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:George_Catlin_-_Os-ce-o-l%C3%A1,_The_Black_Drink,_a_Warrior_of_Great_Distinction_-_1985.66.301_-_Smithsonian_American_Art_Museum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
